  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-01-05T10:28:33.250Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Honestly, I love the Trust System and all personally but, it's not perfect. Today I just witnessed some person crash one of my friends over some petty drama without even using a particle system/shader(I made a report already of course.)\n\nThat being said, would it be possible to implement a two-step verification? I know the downsides and criticisms such method would receive however-- the fact that crashers are still a problem would justify implementing this.\n\nThis method although not a permanent solution, would help alleviate the issues of crashers and so forth that evade IP bans and such.\n\nEDIT:\nTo add on;\nA game called Tom Clancy's Rainbow Six Siege implements this feature requiring 2-step verification in order to play ranked matches. This method is used to \"flush\" out toxic players from the game. I understand VRChat isn't a shooter game however, it could really help.",
